  "content": {
    "text": "2 days ago\nChip stocks bounce back, with SOX seeing unanimous gains\nThe chip sector is seeing a nice bounce ahead of the open, after seeing its worst day in six years on Friday, with all 30 components of the PHLX Semiconductor Index gaining ground.\nOf the SOX's biggest gainers, Marvell's stock was shooting up 8.5%, boosted by its awaited inclusion in the S&P 500, after sinking 16.7% on Friday. And Micron shares were rallying 7.1% after falling 13.3% on Friday.\nThe weakest performer was Qualcomm's stock, which was rising just 2%, after dropping 11% on Friday.",
